# AI Financial Advisor Agent - Cursor Rules

## Project Overview
An AI agent for financial advisors integrating Gmail, Google Calendar, and Hubspot CRM.

## Tech Stack
- Backend: Python 3.11, FastAPI, SQLAlchemy, PostgreSQL, pgvector
- Frontend: React 18, TypeScript, Vite, TailwindCSS
- AI: OpenAI GPT-4, embeddings
- Deployment: Render, Fly.io, Docker

## Code Style

### Python
- Follow PEP 8
- Use type hints
- Async/await for all I/O operations
- Use Pydantic for validation
- Descriptive function names

### TypeScript/React
- Functional components with hooks
- TypeScript strict mode
- Use const for variables
- Destructure props
- TailwindCSS for styling

## Naming Conventions
- Files: snake_case.py, PascalCase.tsx
- Functions: snake_case (Python), camelCase (TS)
- Classes: PascalCase
- Constants: UPPER_SNAKE_CASE
- Components: PascalCase

## Best Practices
- Always handle errors
- Log important operations
- Use environment variables
- Write descriptive comments
- Keep functions small
- DRY principle
- Type everything

## Database
- Use SQLAlchemy async
- Create models in app/models/
- Use UUIDs for primary keys
- Include created_at, updated_at

## API
- RESTful endpoints
- Use Pydantic models
- Return proper status codes
- Include error messages
- Use dependency injection

## Security
- Never commit secrets
- Use environment variables
- Validate all inputs
- Sanitize user data
- Use HTTPS in production

